cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this architecture, the toy reference implementation, or the benchmark results in your own work, please cite it as below."
title: "qpu4qc: Bridging Quantum Chemistry and Quantum Hardware for Real-World Engineering"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Selvaraj"
    given-names: "Selva Chandrasekaran"
repository-code: "https://github.com/selvachandrasekaranselvaraj/qpu4qc"
url: "https://github.com/selvachandrasekaranselvaraj/qpu4qc"
abstract: >
  An architecture for treating density functional theory, machine-learned
  interatomic potentials, and quantum-hardware-computed active-space
  energies as interchangeable, content-addressed, calibrated levels of one
  computation graph - with a runnable toy reference implementation and
  real, measured benchmark results.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum chemistry
  - materials science
  - computational chemistry
  - machine-learned interatomic potentials
  - density functional theory
  - variational quantum eigensolver
  - high performance computing
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
